    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Ebola facilities and beds, DRC 2026\"\nsubtitle: \"Bundibugyo virus disease outbreak: where patients could be treated, and how full it was\"\ndate: last-modified\ndate-format: \"D MMMM YYYY\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n::: {.note}\nThis page summarises a dataset that is still under review. Every figure is\nread by a language model from public situation reports and checked word for\nword against its source, but most rows have not yet been read by a person.\nFacility counts are an upper bound: where two names might be one site they are\ncounted as two until someone who knows the site says otherwise.\n[Data and methods](methods.qmd) has the detail.\n:::\n\n## At a glance\n\nFacilities from INSP situation reports, 14 May to\n13 September 2026. Bed figures from WHO AFRO's weekly reports,\nwhich run later.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Treatment centres (CTE) reported open | 62 |\n| Transit centres (CT) reported open | 33 |\n| Isolation centres (CI) reported open | 8 |\n| Active beds, 20 September (WHO AFRO) | 1,535 |\n| Bed occupancy, 20 September (WHO AFRO) | 59% |\n\nA site counts as open once a report shows it open or holding patients.\n\n\n## Sites open over time\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![Sites reported open or holding patients, by the date a report first showed it. Each line can only rise: a closure is not subtracted. The true opening of most sites is earlier than the line shows, because the first report to mention a site usually finds it already working.](index_files/figure-html/fig-open-1.png){#fig-open fig-alt='Step lines of cumulative sites open by kind, rising from mid-May to mid-September 2026. Hospital isolation and treatment centres grow most.' width=1050}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Beds and patients\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![National active bed capacity and patients in isolation. WHO AFRO figures are weekly; INSP figures are daily and stop in early August, when the bed tables leave the situation reports. Lines break where no figure was published for more than ten days.](index_files/figure-html/fig-beds-1.png){#fig-beds fig-alt='Line chart of bed capacity rising from about 650 in late June to about 1500 in September, with patients in isolation between 700 and 900.' width=1050}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![Bed occupancy by province, where a report gives it. Above the line at 100% a province held more patients than it had beds. Figures are as printed, not recomputed.](index_files/figure-html/fig-occupancy-1.png){#fig-occupancy fig-alt='Small multiple dot-and-line charts of bed occupancy by province. Nord-Kivu is repeatedly above 100 percent; Ituri falls from about 90 to about 45 percent.' width=1050}\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNord-Kivu held more patients than it had beds for most of July, in both the\nINSP daily tables and the WHO AFRO weekly reports. Neither says how: extra\nbeds not yet counted, patients waiting in transit, or a bed count that lagged.\n\n<!-- UNCERTAIN: what occupancy above 100% counts. See DEVLOG item 5. -->\n\n## Treatment centres\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table class=\"data\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Province </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Health zone </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Centre </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Open by </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Latest status </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Beds </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Bas-Uele </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Buta </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> CTE de Buta </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 17 August </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Being built, 22 August </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Haut-Uele </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Boma Mangb